animation-doc-description-animation = The shorthand wires name, duration, easing, delay, iteration count, direction, fill mode and play state into one CSS animation occurrence.
animation-doc-description-animation-name = Selects the @keyframes rule by name. Vizia starts, updates and cancels the CSS animation automatically from computed style.
animation-doc-description-animation-duration = Controls the active interval for one iteration. Negative durations are rejected.
animation-doc-description-animation-delay = Positive and negative delays are supported. A negative delay begins as if the animation had already been running.
animation-doc-description-timing-function = Supports CSS easing keywords, validated cubic-bezier() and steps() timing functions.
animation-doc-description-steps = Discrete timing functions jump between sampled positions instead of interpolating continuously.
animation-doc-description-iteration-count = Finite, fractional and infinite iteration counts are supported. This example runs three times and keeps its final value.
animation-doc-description-direction = normal, reverse, alternate and alternate-reverse affect iteration progress without changing the keyframe data.
animation-doc-description-fill-mode = none, forwards, backwards and both control whether sampled values apply before or after the active phase.
animation-doc-description-play-state = running and paused operate on the same CSS occurrence and preserve local progress when resumed.
animation-doc-description-composition = replace, add and accumulate are resolved inside Vizia's property stores using a stable per-property effect stack.
animation-doc-description-timeline = The effect can be sampled from document time, a named scroll source, scroll() or view() progress.
animation-doc-description-keyframes = from/to and percentage offsets are parsed into the same animation storage used by Rust-side animations and transitions.
animation-doc-description-percentage-keyframes = Multiple offsets, duplicate offsets, implicit endpoints and underlying values are normalized by the CSS animation runtime.
animation-doc-description-multiple = Comma-separated animation lists create independent occurrences. CSS list repetition rules resolve shorter longhand lists.
animation-doc-description-document-timeline = The default document timeline advances from wall-clock time and requests frames only while sampled values are changing.
animation-doc-description-named-scroll = A Vizia ScrollView can publish a named normalized progress source that CSS animations consume directly.
animation-doc-description-scroll = scroll() uses the selected scroll source and axis as the animation clock. Stop scrolling and the animation freezes.
animation-doc-description-view = view() derives progress from the subject entering and leaving its nearest scroll viewport.
animation-doc-description-opacity = Paint-only interpolation. It does not require layout or text reconstruction.
animation-doc-description-transform = Transform lists are sampled through the retransform path rather than layout. Compatible functions interpolate component-by-component.
animation-doc-description-transform-origin = Transform origin is store-backed and participates in the same animation clock as transforms.
animation-doc-description-translate = Individual translate is independently animatable and supports additive effect composition.
animation-doc-description-rotate = Individual rotate is independently animatable and supports add/accumulate composition.
animation-doc-description-scale = Individual scale is independently animatable and participates in transform invalidation.
animation-doc-description-clip-path = Clip path changes use the reclip path. Incompatible shapes fall back deterministically.
animation-doc-description-filter = Compatible filter lists interpolate; incompatible lists use discrete fallback.
animation-doc-description-backdrop-filter = The glass surface changes blur while colored content keeps moving underneath, so the backdrop effect is visually distinct from a normal filter.
animation-doc-description-background-color = Background colors interpolate as paint-only values.
animation-doc-description-background-family = The All tab combines the background stores; the remaining tabs isolate position, size and discrete repeat behavior.
animation-doc-description-border-width = Choose a side (or all four) to see exactly which border-width store is being animated.
animation-doc-description-border-color = Choose a side (or all four) to isolate border-color interpolation.
animation-doc-description-corner-radius = Choose a corner or all corners. The preview uses a large stable surface so the geometry change is obvious.
animation-doc-description-outline = Outline width, color and offset are all backed by animatable stores.
animation-doc-description-shadow = Compatible shadow lists interpolate and redraw without relayout.
animation-doc-description-color = Font color is a paint-only text property and does not reconstruct text layout.
animation-doc-description-font-size = Font size animation requests text reconstruction because glyph metrics change.
animation-doc-description-letter-spacing = Letter spacing is reflow-affecting and uses the text construction path.
animation-doc-description-line-height = Line height is reflow-affecting and shares the animation clock with other text properties.
animation-doc-description-text-paint = These text paint stores are animatable without text reconstruction.
animation-doc-description-fill = The fill color store is animatable and redraw-only. The preview uses a real SVG.
animation-doc-description-position = Position offsets are layout-affecting. The runtime only requests relayout when the sampled value actually changes.
animation-doc-description-padding = All four padding stores are animatable and layout-affecting.
animation-doc-description-gap = Row/column gaps are animatable layout values and participate in change-aware relayout ticking.
animation-doc-description-size = Width and height support keyframe interpolation, including the existing auto-size animation resolution path.
animation-doc-description-constraints = Constraint stores and min/max horizontal/vertical gap stores participate in CSS animation playback.
animation-doc-description-display = Display is store-backed but fundamentally discrete rather than numerically interpolated.
animation-doc-description-custom-properties = Typed Vizia custom property families use the same animation/composition machinery as built-in properties.
animation-doc-description-runtime-controls = Runtime control operates on the same stable CSS occurrence and the same property-store clocks that render the effect.
animation-doc-description-blur-popover = A native Vizia Popover can use the same CSS animation engine for a short entrance effect.
animation-doc-description-throbber = Reusable loading indicators cover staggered dots, a rotating ring, equalizer bars, an orbit and a pulse.
animation-doc-description-skeleton = Reusable skeleton compositions share one animated bone primitive and expose common content-layout variants.
animation-doc-description-svg-morph = Tabler heart, star and bolt icons cross-morph through coordinated opacity, scale and rotation while preserving native SVG rendering.
